        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Dashboard: workspace time-travel + blame",
        "body": "> 📦 **Part of the modular-dashboard package** — master hub **#101136** (architecture diagrams · bottom-up merge order · the full per-PR test map).\n>\n> 🧪 **Try this PR:** open workspace history, scrub versions, and click a widget's provenance → the version diff renders and provenance deep-links to the logbook session (#99930).\n\n---\n\n# Dashboard: workspace time-travel + blame\n\n> Scrub your dashboard through its own history, diff any snapshot against now (grouped by who changed what), and click a widget to jump to the agent session that created it.\n\nCloses #101822. **Stacked on #101098** — targets `main` with a cumulative diff; review the history RPCs, `history.ts`, and the panel/blame UI as the delta.\n\n## What's in this PR\n- **Read-only history RPCs** — `dashboard.workspace.history.list` / `.get` (both `operator.read`) over the existing 20-entry undo ring. `list` returns `{ version, savedAt, bytes }` newest-first (metadata only, never bodies); `get(version)` returns one snapshot.\n- **History panel** — a toolbar button opens a modal: the version list, a read-only preview render of any snapshot, a **diff vs current** grouped by actor (tab/widget added / removed / moved / retitled), and **restore** (wired to the existing single-step `dashboard.workspace.undo`, offered only on the newest snapshot).\n- **Blame** — the cell menu shows \"created by `agent:main` · vN\"; for agent authors it links to the logbook (#99930) when that tab is advertised, so the dashboard becomes auditable and the logbook gains a spatial index.\n\n## How it works\nEverything is a **read-only** surface over state that already existed: the undo ring (snapshots), `workspaceVersion`, and `createdBy` provenance. The ring-read API parses ring files without mutating them; restore reuses the existing undo write (no new write RPC); the diff indexes widgets by id and tabs by slug across two docs. No new dependency, no new write privilege.\n\n**Honest limitations (called out in-code):** restore is single-step (the ring is an undo ring, so only the most recent change is revertible); the logbook is a day-keyed snapshot journal with no URL-addressable session/day, so blame links to the logbook tab root rather than a specific entry; first-seen version resolves only once snapshot bodies are loaded (the panel), falling back to provenance-only.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n**Behavior or issue addressed:** When agents co-edit an operator's dashboard, \"what changed, who changed it, and why\" had no answer — despite the substrate recording everything needed (undo ring, versions, provenance). This exposes it: history scrub, actor-grouped diff, restore, and widget→logbook blame.\n**Evidence:** `node scripts/test-projects.mjs extensions/dashboard` green (ring metadata/snapshot reads, RPC read-scope) + `pnpm vitest run src/lib/dashboard src/pages/plugin` green (history loaders, `computeWorkspaceDiff` add/remove/move cases, `groupDiffByActor`, blame first-seen + graceful fallback); `ui:i18n:check`, `ui:build`, full oxlint clean. Counts verified by the submitting orchestrator's own gate: `extensions/dashboard` 83, UI dashboard + plugin-page + cell suites 138.\n\n",
